    {
      "id": "s04",
      "type": "DSA_COST",
      "narration": "Scanning means checking every item until you hit the one you're after. On ten items that's up to ten checks, which is nothing at all. On a million it's up to a million, and on a billion it's a billion. Binary search does four checks on ten items, twenty on a million, and thirty on a billion. Look hard at those last two, because going from a million to a billion, a thousand times the data, costs you ten extra guesses. That's what logarithmic means in practice.",
